== Notes ==
* {{i|Mega Blast|anr}} only gains 3 charges per battery.
* {{dlc|a+}} Batteries charge only the current active item, if holding multiple.
** {{dlc|r}} If Isaac has an active item in the consumable slot, batteries prefer to charge the active item slot first.
* {{dlc|r}} Micro Batteries can spawn in room layouts even if they have not been unlocked yet.
* {{dlc|r}} If Golden Batteries have not been unlocked yet, they will be replaced by a random Battery pickup in any room layouts containing them.
* {{dlc|r}} {{I|Holy Mantle}} and similar effects will block the damage from the Golden Battery, allowing for infinite usage of active items on that floor.
* {{dlc+|r}} Golden Batteries can re-appear in undiscovered rooms, including the {{r|Secret Room}}.
** It can re-appear in any previously visited rooms '''that are displayed on the map''', even in the mirrored area where {{I|Knife Piece 1}} is located, in the abandoned area where {{I|Knife Piece 2}} is located, or in the Death Certificate path
** It can't appear in any room that is not displayed on the map at anytime, like {{r|Crawl Space}}, {{r|Black Market}}, {{s|Downpour}} entrance, {{s|Mines}} entrance, {{r|I AM ERROR}} room.{{dlc-}}
* The probabilities in the table refer to the kind of battery that is generated by the game when a battery pickup is spawned with a sub-type of 0 (i.e. a random battery).
* {{dlc|nr}} Items / pickups with the {{i|D20}} effect can reroll batteries, but can't reroll other pickups into batteries.
* Batteries can be randomly spawned by {{i|Spider Mod}}.

